{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "purpose": "Maintainer stability classification for the 1.0 public SDK surface. scripts/generate-one-point-zero-inventory.mjs reads this file for each symbol's and subpath's decision; without an entry a symbol stays undecided.",
  "classifiedOn": "2026-08-05",
  "classifiedBy": "apet97",
  "approvedDecisions": [
    "stable",
    "experimental",
    "deprecated",
    "internal"
  ],
  "method": "A symbol is classified stable when it is exercised by real evidence: a CLI or MCP call site, a shipped example, reference documentation, or a wrapper test. Evidence counts below are file counts gathered mechanically, not hand-entered. Error classes and helper families are classified as families -- splitting NotFoundError from ForbiddenError by call-site count would be arbitrary, because the family is one contract.",
  "notes": [
    "entityChangesExperimental is a client property rather than an exported symbol, so it is not listed here. It keeps its in-code @experimental and @beta tags because Clockify's own entity-changes API is experimental.",
    "INVOICE_EDITABLE_FIELDS was the only symbol with no evidence of any kind. It is now pinned against invoiceUpdateBodyFromExisting by wrapper/tests/invoice-body.test.ts, so the constant and the body the SDK actually sends cannot drift apart.",
    "All 28 subpaths are kept at 1.0, including the 13 that export exactly one symbol (composed-fetch, create-client, deprecation, health, iter, expense-list, otel-hooks, pagination, webhooks, webhook-events, with-response, diagnostics, bulk). Merging them was weighed and rejected on measured evidence. Every one of the 13 already has at least one importer in wrapper/examples, wrapper/tests, cli/src, mcp/src or wrapper/README.md, so none is speculative, and wrapper/.size-limit.json holds a per-subpath byte ceiling, so the granularity is measured rather than accidental. The clearest case is the observability trio: health is 1.2 kB, otel-hooks 4.0 kB and diagnostics 8.2 kB of built ESM, so folding them into one subpath would grow a health-only import to 13.4 kB. The package ships dual ESM/CJS and CJS does not tree-shake, so a CJS consumer would pay that in full. A subpath is frozen by 1.0, so this decision is recorded as intent rather than left as an accident of history."
  ],
